{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat upon the blood</b> — Scripture placed this commandment adjacent to the commandment of orlah, to allude to what they of blessed memory said (Midrash Talphiot, Bereshit Rabbah 21:7) that Adam the first man sinned in eating of the Tree of Knowledge before the time of its permissibility, which is the aspect of orlah, for had he waited until the eve of holy Shabbat he would have sanctified over the wine. And this is the sod of their words of blessed memory when they said (Sanhedrin 38b): Adam was drawing along in his orlah — this is his orlah. And this is what the verse states in proximity to the warning ״וַעֲרַלְתֶּם עָרְלָתוֹ״ — <b>לֹא תֹאכְלוּ</b>, meaning, of the fruit of orlah; <b>עַל הַדָּם</b>, meaning, on account of the blood, for this is the cause of all shedding of blood — the blood of man and the blood of his seed. And you should know that the cause of the orlahs and their essential root is this — their source, for aside from Adam's sin there would have been no orlah in the world, neither of plant life nor of living creatures."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:59:24.177848592Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}